        "cnm_139"
      ],
      "explanation": "Let \\(M\\) be the midpoint of hypotenuse \\(AB\\). The right-triangle median property makes \\(CM\\) equal to the known length \\(AC\\):\n\\[\nAM=CM=\\frac{AB}{2}=3=AC.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\triangle AMC\\) is equilateral, so \\(\\angle CAM=60^\\circ\\). Since \\(M\\) lies on segment \\(AB\\), \\(\\angle A=\\angle CAM=60^\\circ\\).",
      "id": "hypotenuse-midpoint",
